    "narrative": "The LawDog lineup is headlined today by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (80.87) and **Bryce Harper** (78.75), who provide the structural foundation for our daily scoring. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** draws a favorable matchup against Mitch Keller (xERA 5.13), where his high base projection is bolstered by an elite SP skill matchup. Simultaneously, **Bryce Harper** benefits significantly from a park factor boost (+16%) and a favorable matchup against Kyle Bradish, though his outlook is tempered by a 41% rain risk. **Lawrence Butler** (73.47) rounds out our elite options, leveraging a strong platoon advantage against Keider Montero to anchor our middle-order production.\n\nStrategic emphasis on stolen bases continues to influence our deployment of **Masyn Winn** (64.31) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (61.81). **Masyn Winn** is positioned for potential activity on the basepaths due to the slow delivery profile of Max Scherzer, while **Jung Hoo Lee**\u2014assuming a #2 spot\u2014maintains solid efficiency despite the challenge of Michael King. Notably, **Gleyber Torres** (65.79) earns a start thanks to an aggressive +13% adjustment for his platoon advantage against Gage Jump, effectively capitalizing on the favorable park conditions.\n\nThe tightest decision on the bench involved **Drew Gilbert** (49.63), who fell just shy of cracking the lineup. While **Drew Gilbert** shares the same advantageous matchup against Michael King as several of our starters, his projected slotting at the bottom of the order (-3%) forced him into the reserve role. We are monitoring significant weather risks for **Bryce Harper**, **Dylan Beavers**, and **JJ Bleday**, all of whom carry precipitation concerns; should these games be delayed or postponed, we will be forced to rotate in bench options to ensure we remain within our game cap limits while protecting our efficiency.",
